#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Panimula"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the previous lesson, we took a first look at quantum error correction, focusing specifically on the 9-qubit Shor code.\n"
"In this lesson, we'll introduce the *stabilizer formalism*, which is a mathematical framework through which a broad class of quantum error correcting codes, known as *stabilizer codes*, can be specified and analyzed.\n"
"This includes the 9-qubit Shor code along with many other examples, including codes that seem likely to be well-suited to real-world quantum devices.\n"
"Not every quantum error correcting code is a stabilizer code, but many are, including every example that we'll see in this course.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa nakaraang aralin, unang tiningnan natin ang quantum error correction, na nakatuon lalo na sa 9-qubit Shor code.\n"
"Sa araling ito, ipapakilala natin ang *stabilizer formalism*, na isang mathematical framework kung saan maaaring tukuyin at suriin ang malawak na klase ng quantum error correcting codes, na kilala bilang *stabilizer codes*.\n"
"Kasama dito ang 9-qubit Shor code pati na rin ang maraming iba pang halimbawa, kabilang ang mga code na tila angkop para sa mga tunay na quantum device.\n"
"Hindi lahat ng quantum error correcting code ay stabilizer code, ngunit marami ang ganoon, kasama na ang bawat halimbawa na makikita natin sa kursong ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The lesson begins with a short discussion of Pauli matrices, and tensor products of Pauli matrices more generally, which can represent not only operations on qubits, but also measurements of qubits — in which case they're typically referred to as *observables*.\n"
"We'll then go back and take a second look at the repetition code and see how it can be described in terms of Pauli matrix observables.\n"
"This will both inform and lead into a general discussion of stabilizer codes, including several examples, basic properties of stabilizer codes, and how the fundamental tasks of encoding, detecting errors, and correcting those errors can be performed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nagsisimula ang aralin sa maikling talakayan ng mga Pauli matrix, at ng mga tensor product ng Pauli matrices sa pangkalahatan, na kayang kumatawan hindi lamang sa mga operasyon sa qubits, kundi pati na rin sa pagsukat sa mga qubit — na sa ganitong kaso ay karaniwang tinutukoy bilang *observables*.\n"
"Babalik tayo at muling titingnan ang repetition code at makikita kung paano ito mailarawan gamit ang mga Pauli matrix observable.\n"
"Magbibigay ito ng pundasyon at magdadala sa atin sa isang pangkalahatang talakayan ng stabilizer codes, kasama ang ilang halimbawa, mga pangunahing katangian ng stabilizer codes, at kung paano isasagawa ang mga pangunahing gawain ng pag-encode, pag-detect ng mga error, at pagwawasto ng mga ito.\n"

